snp4.8:10.1 starts: Whom would you gain as opponent, Pasūra,
snp4.8:10.2 starts: among those who live above confrontation—
snp4.8:10.3 starts: not pitting view against view—
snp4.8:10.4 starts: who have nothing here grasped as supreme?
snp4.3:6.1 starts: Because entrenchments in views
snp4.3:6.2 starts: when considering what’s grasped
snp4.3:6.3 starts: that’s why
snp4.3:6.4 starts: in light of these very
snp4.4:4.1 starts: Abandoning what’s first,
snp4.4:4.2 starts: Following perturbation,
snp4.4:4.3 starts: They embrace & reject
snp4.4:4.4 starts: —like a monkey releasing a branch
snp4.4:6.1 starts: He’s enemy-free
snp4.4:6.2 starts: seen, heard, or sensed.
snp4.4:6.3 starts: By whom, with what,
snp4.4:6.4 starts: —one who has seen in this way,
snp4.5:7.1 starts: hasn’t the least
snp4.5:7.2 starts: with regard to what’s seen, heard, or sensed.
snp4.5:7.3 starts: By whom, with what,
snp4.5:7.4 starts: —this brahman
snp4.6:2.1 starts: People grieve
snp4.6:2.2 starts: for nothing possessed is constant,
snp4.6:2.3 starts: Seeing this separation
snp4.6:2.4 starts: one shouldn’t follow the household life.
snp4.7:1.1 starts: Tissa-metteyya:
snp4.7:1.3 starts: for one given over
snp4.7:1.4 starts: Having heard your teaching,
snp4.7:1.5 starts: we’ll train in seclusion.”
snp4.7:10.1 starts: People enmeshed
snp4.7:10.2 starts: a sage remote,
snp4.7:10.3 starts: leading his life
snp4.7:10.4 starts: —one who’s crossed over the flood.”
snp4.8:4.1 starts: He whose doctrine is [judged as] demolished,
snp4.8:4.2 starts: defeated, by those judging the issue:
snp4.8:4.3 starts: He laments, he grieves—the inferior exponent.
snp4.8:4.4 starts: ‘He beat me,’ he mourns.
